IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa14-types`
IMPORT `pa14-state-pension`
IMPORT `pa14-deferral`
IMPORT `pa14-bereavement`

-- Pensions Act 2014 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "Which state pension is this person entitled to and at what weekly rate;
--    what does deferring it add; and are they entitled to bereavement
--    support payment?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Pension case` HAS
    `the pension facts`                                 IS A `Pension facts`
    `a deferral`                                        IS A MAYBE `Deferral facts`
    `a bereavement`                                     IS A MAYBE `Bereavement facts`

DECLARE `Pension position` HAS
    `kind of state pension`                             IS A `Kind of state pension`
    `weekly state pension`                              IS A NUMBER
    `whole weeks deferred`                              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `weekly increase for deferral`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `entitled to bereavement support payment`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref ss 1-5, 17, 30, 31, Sch 1
@export default The position under the Pensions Act 2014 (UK) for one person: which state pension under Part 1 they are entitled to on reaching pensionable age (none, full, reduced or transitional) and its weekly rate; if they deferred it, the whole weeks deferred and the weekly increase (s 17); and, if a partner died, whether they are entitled to bereavement support payment (ss 30-31). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Pension case`  @desc The pension facts, any deferral, and any bereavement
GIVETH A `Pension position`
`the pension position for` c MEANS
    `Pension position` WITH
        `kind of state pension`                         IS `the kind of state pension for` p
        `weekly state pension`                          IS `the weekly state pension for` p
        `whole weeks deferred`                          IS
            CONSIDER c's `a deferral`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the whole weeks deferred in` f)
        `weekly increase for deferral`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `a deferral`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the weekly increase for deferral in` f)
        `entitled to bereavement support payment`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `a bereavement`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST b  THEN JUST (`is entitled to bereavement support payment` b)
    WHERE
        p MEANS c's `the pension facts`
